    summary: "Peer review currently scores significance, innovation and approach, which reward novelty and technical elegance. A burden criterion (deaths, DALYs and unmet need in the target population, plausible time to patient impact) is scored separately by a panel that includes trained patient reviewers and carries 20% of the total. The Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute and the US Department of Defense cancer programmes already include consumer reviewers; this makes burden an explicit, weighted term.",
